// States put back together, and peoples brought under one roof.
//
// The 2024 map is full of countries split in two or three - Cyprus, Moldova and Transnistria,
// Georgia and its two breakaways, Somalia and Somaliland, the Yemens, the Libyas, the Syrias,
// the Sudans - and every side of every one of them claims to be the real country. Any of them
// can put it back together and proclaim it under the old name: Transnistria that holds all of
// Moldova proclaims Moldova, as the Republic of Moldova would. The territory is the authored
// 2024 ground of every piece, so it is done by treaty or by war, never by a button.
//
// Below them, the kin unions the year argued about - Serbia and Montenegro again, Albania and
// Kosovo.
//
// The last block opens the Arab projects to every Arab side, not only to the recognised
// states: Hamas or a Syrian faction that holds the ground can proclaim them as Egypt could.
// Entries naming an existing id change only the fields they name.
